  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2d1e83780892b5c4592add1c4998da52, type: 3}
  m_Name: MusicFacts
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FactPack
  category: 8
  facts:
  - Beethoven was deaf when he composed the Ninth Symphony.
  - Mozart composed his first music at age five.
  - The Beatles are the best-selling band of all time.
  - A piano has 88 keys.
  - The most expensive instrument ever sold is a Stradivarius violin.
  - Queen's 'Bohemian Rhapsody' has no chorus.
  - ABBA's members are from Sweden.
  - Bob Dylan won the Nobel Prize in Literature.
  - Elvis Presley never wrote any of his own songs.
  - Jimi Hendrix couldn't read music.
  - The harmonica is the world's best-selling instrument.
  - Michael Jackson's 'Thriller' is the best-selling album.
  - The first song ever played in space was 'Jingle Bells'.
